msgid "Open MyWhoosh and go to the <b>Connections</b> screen."
msgstr ""

msgid "Click the <b>OpenBikeControl</b> icon at the top right."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Choose <b>Click2Whoosh</b>. MyWhoosh asks whether to connect (“OpenBikeControl Instance Found”): press "
"<b>YES</b>."
msgstr ""

msgid "You can also do this later: Click2Whoosh keeps listening for as long as it is open."
msgstr ""

msgid "The buttons"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This is how they are set now. A button can do one thing with a click, another with a double click and "
"another one if you hold it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Try them now: with this window in front, the buttons light up on the drawing and send nothing to MyWhoosh "
"or to the music."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To save battery, the Click turns itself off when you are not using it and MyWhoosh is closed. The first "
"button you press wakes it up (that press is lost)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Menu and settings"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Click2Whoosh has no windows or Dock icon: you will find it in the menu bar at the top right, as a cyclist. "
"The icon is solid when the Click is connected and lighter when it is waiting for it. Click it to open the "
"menu."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To change what the buttons do: choose a button (by clicking it on the drawing or pressing it on the Click) "
"and decide what it does with a click, a double click and a long press. It saves by itself."
msgstr ""

msgid "Advanced"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"At the bottom of Settings: how long a long press lasts, how fast to double-click, at what percentage to "
"warn about a low battery, the sound on every shift and the use of the left Click."
msgstr ""

